   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     57,
     73
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests that templates containing malformed or unresolvable variable syntax are returned unchanged. The cases fall into four categories: <ul> <li>Empty / blank variable names — the substitutor skips \"${}\", \"${ }\", etc. because an empty key can never match a map entry.</li> <li>Incomplete delimiters — a lone \"${\" or lone \"}\" is not a complete variable reference, so nothing is substituted.</li> <li>Escape-only constructs — patterns such as \"${${}}\" consist entirely of the escape character or unresolvable nested prefixes and produce no output change.</li> <li>Nested-prefix constructs — patterns like \"${${\" or \"${${ }}\" open a second prefix before finding a suffix, leaving the whole expression unresolved.</li> </ul>"
   },
